  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mo>&#168;</mo></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>&nbsp;(Aliphatic amines) Most basic due to +I effect of methyl group. Methoxy group is&nbsp;electron donating group and increase electron density by (+M) effect on&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;group.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"171\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/image9-0f57d4f4-8cc9-4064-87b0-537158b9fc1d.jpg\" width=\"125\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group withdraws electron density from N of <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;and decrease basic strength.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"181\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/image10-064c2962-4b03-4858-9c8f-6689bcc1818c.jpg\" width=\"99\" /><br />&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mo>&#168;</mo></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> Most basic because NH<sub>2</sub> connected with sp<sup>3</sup> C while in i,ii&amp;iii Connected with sp<sup>2</sup> C &amp; basic strength <math> <mo>&#8733;</mo> </math> +M/+I<br /><br />basic strength <math> <mo>&#8733;</mo> </math> <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mtext>M</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mtext>I</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />NO<sub>2</sub> exert -M so least basic while -OCH<sub>3</sub> exert +M so more basic.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0102096-1.JPG\" style=\"width: 275px; height: 160px;\" /><br /><br />M effect is a stronger effect than&nbsp;the I effect.</p><p>Aliphatic amines are more basic than aromatic amines because in aliphatic amines lone pair of electrons on&nbsp;nitrogen is localized and easy to donate, while in aromatic amines lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom is delocalized and participate in resonance.</p>",
